iddle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years, the same count as November to December. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, August to September came in at 42% of normal and June to July at 155%. So far in 2026, April to May sits at 151% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 24744 at 45% of normal.</p>"}
